Generate from Cott contracts; preserve declared types, errors, effects, and invariants.
CottList: iterate directly; Option: use isinstance, not match.
Implement each callable's documented behavior using the standard library and distributions selected by uv.lock for its declared effects. Database and network effects permit direct use of those drivers; a separate Cott facade is not required for native SDK operations.
Implementation imports may use cott_runtime, exact generated *_types modules, and declared callable facades present in the selected prompt context. Never import cott_bindings, _cott_impl, or other project-local modules; do not invent undeclared Cott helper callables.
Do not substitute empty catalogs or unconditional failures for real backend operations. Return declared errors only for the documented validation condition or a genuine attempted operation failure; never include credentials or complete connection endpoints in error messages.
cott-domain real.harlequin.catalog.refresh_catalog return: After isinstance on raw dict/list/tuple data, cast to typed object containers before iteration and validate entries before narrowing; no Unknown containers. Remove a cast when its expression already has type object, including Opaque.unwrap(). Narrow required SDK strings explicitly; use concrete SDK cursor/metadata types and check optional values. Narrow Nebula Name into a local str before append. Use a direct final else for exhaustive AdapterKind branching. Preserve canonical return types and never suppress type errors.
cott-domain real.harlequin.catalog.refresh_catalog error: For SDK metadata typing: annotate SQL helper query parameters as typing.LiteralString when callers pass fixed SQL literals (psycopg rejects general str). Cast PyMySQL conn.cursor() to its concrete pymysql.cursors.Cursor before assigning/using it. ADBC depth is Literal["db_schemas", "tables"]. The pinned pyarrow.RecordBatchReader name itself is untyped: represent its documented context-manager protocol as cast(contextlib.AbstractContextManager[object], conn.adbc_get_objects(...)), then use with to obtain an object accepted by duckdb.from_arrow and guarantee reader closure. Do not import pyarrow solely for an Unknown annotation. Cast BigQuery list_tables' iterator to Iterable[google.cloud.bigquery.table.TableListItem] before iteration, and normalize its untyped table_type property with cast(str|None, table.table_type). Cast Databricks cursor.description to object or Sequence[Sequence[object]] | None at the boundary before passing it to a shape-checking helper. These casts describe documented SDK data and preserve runtime validation; they do not suppress diagnostics or replace canonical return types.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.begin_transaction return: Connection.session is already an Opaque by the facade ABI; do not repeat isinstance(Opaque). Still check its tag and validate unwrap()'s object payload. After isinstance(raw,dict), cast to dict[str,object] before keys/values/indexing or returning it, and validate the exact string key set and each value. Do not leave dict[Unknown,Unknown].
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.commit_transaction return: The facade already checks Opaque wrapper types; validate tags/payloads without redundant isinstance(Opaque). Cast raw checked dict to dict[str,object] before keys/indexing/return. After checking ExitStack, narrow it with cast(contextlib.ExitStack[bool|None], value), matching the cleanup helper's fully parameterized annotation. Preserve all lease/driver checks, actual commit, failure cleanup and closed-state behavior.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.rollback_transaction return: The facade already checks Opaque wrapper types; validate tags/payloads without redundant isinstance(Opaque). Cast raw checked dict to dict[str,object] before keys/indexing/return. After checking ExitStack, narrow it with cast(contextlib.ExitStack[bool|None], value), matching the cleanup helper's fully parameterized annotation. Preserve actual rollback and ownership checks.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.disconnect return: After isinstance(raw,dict), cast to dict[str,object] before keys/indexing or assignment to payload. Use direct else for the final exhaustive AdapterKind variant, not a redundant isinstance. Keep tag/metadata/driver/lock validation and actual rollback/cleanup.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.connect return: Normalize decoded JSON containers to dict[str,object]/list[object] via cast after shape checks before iteration/indexing, then validate members. Compare typed set[str] key sets to set[str], not set[Unknown] to frozenset. DuckDB config annotation is dict[str,str|bool|int|float|list[str]]. Do not expand dict[str,object] into MySQL's typed constructor: pass explicit narrowed host/user/password/database/port/TLS keywords. Cast conn.cursor() to concrete pymysql.cursors.Cursor. NoHostAvailable.errors may be None; narrow a nonnull mapping to Mapping[object,object] before iterating exceptions. For ADBC catalog discovery, use the returned reader's documented AbstractContextManager[object] protocol and duckdb.from_arrow rather than untyped pyarrow table calls; query catalog_name and close the reader/bridge. Preserve live SDK sessions and ExitStack ownership, not probe-and-close.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.execute_sql return: Handle memoryview separately from bytes/bytearray, explicitly cast(memoryview[int], value) before byte conversion; an isinstance narrowing alone leaves memoryview[Unknown]. Do not change SQL or transaction behavior.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.execute_statements return: Avoid a heterogeneous union of DBAPI cursor types: keep concrete per-driver branches and normalize their documented result data at the SDK boundary. Psycopg connections/cursors are parameterized with tuple[object,...]; intentionally supplied whole SQL can use UTF-8 bytes. Cast untyped descriptions and row sequences to object containers before iteration, then validate and build tuple[object,...] rows. BigQuery rows use Iterable[google.cloud.bigquery.table.Row], Cassandra results use Iterable[tuple[object,...]], and Nebula ResultSet.as_primitive uses validated list[dict[str,object]]. Check SDK optional values before access, but do not compare always-present DuckDB description against None. Cast checked opaque payload dict before keys/indexing; do not redundantly test known Opaque wrappers. Use direct else for the final AdapterKind branch. Cast memoryview[int] before bytes conversion, fully parameterize ExitStack, and preserve retained live sessions, actual transactions, row bounds and all eleven real backend paths.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.load_query_file return: After FileLocation_Local, use the remaining S3 branch directly without redundant isinstance. Normalize boto3's untyped response and Body.read result at the SDK boundary using concrete bytes/object annotations before decoding; do not pass Unknown into bytes.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.save_query_file return: After FileLocation_Local, use the remaining S3 branch directly without redundant isinstance. Preserve actual I/O and declared error behavior.
cott-domain real.harlequin.render.export_result return: Use direct final branches for exhaustive ExportFormat_Sql and FileLocation_S3, not redundant isinstance. The boto3 SDK is untyped: assign sdk: Any = boto3 and client: Any = sdk.client("s3") as the existing contract states, so Unknown does not escape calls; preserve typed canonical inputs/results and real serialization/write behavior.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.connect error: The final exhaustive adapter branch is Adbc; use it directly without another isinstance(Adbc) or unreachable fallback.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.execute_statements error: MySQL's Connection is not generic; only psycopg.Connection has a row parameter. Normalize untyped SDK metadata with cast(object, expression) before assignment and validation. Use concrete Cassandra ResultSet and validated Nebula object containers; avoid tautological None checks on BigQuery schema and unused variant imports. Crucially, DuckDBPyConnection.cursor() creates a DUPLICATE connection with independent transaction state. Execute/fetch directly on the retained DuckDB driver used by begin_transaction, and never close that borrowed driver after a statement. A duplicate cursor makes rollback ineffective even though all calls succeed. Preserve same-session transaction semantics for every adapter.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.load_query_file error: boto3 and botocore untyped expressions stay Unknown despite an object annotation. In the ClientError handler, write error_info = cast(object, exc.response.get("Error", {})) before the dict shape check; the annotation error_info: object alone is insufficient. Validate actual response data and preserve declared error mapping and output types.
cott-domain real.harlequin.render.export_result error: Explicitly cast untyped boto3 response fields to object or their documented concrete scalar type before str()/int(); assigning an annotation alone does not eliminate Unknown. Preserve real I/O and declared result types.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.commit_transaction error: Session payload transaction stores the raw unique lease object, NOT its Opaque wrapper. Check transaction.lease.tag == "harlequin.transaction", then compare state["transaction"] is transaction.lease.unwrap(). Comparing it with transaction.lease itself rejects every valid lease. Retain all live-session, active, stale and wrong-owner checks and invoke the actual driver commit.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.rollback_transaction error: Session payload transaction stores the raw unique lease object, NOT its Opaque wrapper. Check transaction.lease.tag == "harlequin.transaction", then compare state["transaction"] is transaction.lease.unwrap(). Retain all ownership/active/closed checks, call the real driver rollback, and keep the same Opaque lease in the inactive returned Transaction.
cott-domain real.harlequin.core.run return: When narrowing a closed union such as Cell or SqlClientError with isinstance chains, handle the last remaining variant in a final else branch without another isinstance check; BasedPyright rejects an isinstance on an already fully narrowed type (reportUnnecessaryIsInstance). Keep the exact prompt signature def run(arguments: CottList[str]) -> Never with CottList imported from cott_runtime and Never from typing; never annotate list[str] or NoReturn.
